From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:58:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2764: keep the TDM clock error masked on
 dancing amplifiers

ASoC unmutes a codec in prepare, before the CPU DAI starts the bus clock
at trigger. Since the J604's six SN012776 amplifiers got the shutdown
dance, whose init step puts them in immediate SDZ mode, each of them
latches a TDM clock error at every stream start, and the driver, which
unmasks every INT_LTCH0 source, takes the shared fault interrupt and
logs "fault: bad TDM clock" at critical level. The J604's journal has
no amplifier line at all in 17 boots before that change and the rate-
limited burst at the first stream of every boot since.

macOS does the same dance, but its amplifier init writes none of the
interrupt mask registers, so the clock error stays masked as at reset,
and it never reads the latches at a stream's start.

Keep the TDM clock error masked on amplifiers that do the shutdown
dance. Over temperature, over current and the other sources stay
unmasked, so the SDZ group still shuts down on a real fault.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
index cc1df5d5d7..403b98f676 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2764.c
@@ -119,6 +119,8 @@ struct tas2764_priv {
 /* LTCH0 faults that shut the whole SDZ group down: over temperature, over current */
 #define TAS2764_INT_LTCH0_GROUP_FAULTS	(BIT(0) | BIT(1))
 #define TAS2764_INT_LTCH0_TDM_CLOCK	BIT(2)
+/* The mask bit of the same source in INT_MASK0 */
+#define TAS2764_INT_MASK0_TDM_CLOCK	BIT(2)
 
 /*
  * With apple,deferred-shutdown, how long after a stream's end the muted amp
@@ -1155,7 +1157,17 @@ static int tas2764_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *component)
 	tas2764->idle_slot_config.tx_mode = SND_SOC_DAI_TDM_IDLE_NONE;
 
 	if (tas2764->irq) {
-		ret = snd_soc_component_write(tas2764->component, TAS2764_INT_MASK0, 0x00);
+		/*
+		 * ASoC unmutes the amplifier before the CPU DAI starts the bus
+		 * clock, and with the shutdown dance's immediate SDZ it latches a
+		 * TDM clock error at every stream start (and can latch it again
+		 * once cleared while the clock is still stopped). macOS, which
+		 * does the dance, leaves the interrupt masks at reset, where that
+		 * error is masked: keep it masked on those amplifiers too.
+		 */
+		ret = snd_soc_component_write(tas2764->component, TAS2764_INT_MASK0,
+					      tas2764_shutdown_dance(tas2764) ?
+					      TAS2764_INT_MASK0_TDM_CLOCK : 0x00);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			goto err_sdz;
 
-- 
